        "raw": "<p style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; line-height: normal;\">Since Daniel Lew&#39;s Sentinels randomizer is only available for androad, I&#39;ve decided to make a randomizer for iOS. &nbsp;You can get it here:&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(</span><a class=\"imgScanned\" href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/sentinels-multiverse-randomizer/id791098197?mt=8&amp;ign-mpt=uo%3D4\" style=\"font-size: 13px; color: rgb(51, 102, 153);\">https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/sentinels-multiverse-randomizer/id791098197?mt=8&amp;ign-mpt=uo%3D4</a><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">)</span></p><p style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: normal;\"><font size=\"2\">The Randomizer uses a point based system to estimate difficulty levels. The system is similar to the SotM score system (</font><a class=\"imgScanned\" href=\"http://x.gray.org/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-difficulty-scores.html\" style=\"font-size: small; color: rgb(51, 102, 153);\">http://x.gray.org/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-difficulty-scores.htm</a>l<font size=\"2\">), but uses a slightly different statistical model.</font></p><p style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; line-height: normal;\">If you have any questions, comments, or suggestions, let me know.</p><p style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; line-height: normal;\">Screenshot: http://imgur.com/WcTKndO</p>",
